spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-4-Goal: In the production messaging drawer, no message a user 
sends is lost or duplicated across network and Realtime outages, reloads, several tabs, account changes, and several 
devices; typing, unread/read state, and @mention notifications stay live and correct; and messaging health is 
observable through redacted logs — without regressing existing messaging.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-5-Plan version: 4
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:6:Highest task ID reserved: T28
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:7:Replanned because: owner decision D9 (state.md, 2026-10-07) — 
the T4 performer found that baseline `public.conversation_members` policies/grants let any authenticated user enrol 
themselves in any conversation or move their row to another conversation through the Data API, defeating every 
members-only rule; owner chose to fix it in this phase. Adds T28; v3 preserved as `reviews/PLAN-v3-reviewed.md`.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-8-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:9:## Standing rules for every task
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-10-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-11-- **Migration rule (BR-014, AC-034):** during the phase a 
migration is done when it is written, applied to the LOCAL database, its tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded 
in the migration header and TRACK. Each one gets a row in 
`spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T23.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-12-- **Old-build compatibility at introduction (§10):** every task 
that changes a DB contract or a route proves, with integration tests against the migrated local DB, that the hosted 
pre-Phase-4 client contract (unkeyed creates) and the Phase 4 client contract (keyed text/attachment/voice creates and 
their replays, without the new fields) keep working; T21 repeats this as a combined smoke with the real old builds.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-13-- **Online application method (T23 only):** the Phase 4 method 
(Phase 4 TRACK T2/T25): re-check `npx supabase migration list --linked` and the target catalog immediately before; 
apply only each reviewed file's SQL transactionally and record only its version; read back by statement hash plus 
catalog objects; smoke-check. Never `supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-14-- **Supabase/RLS review gate (AC-035):** every migration, 
RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs 
supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role never replacing membership checks) before the task is 
done.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-15-- **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** each task's diff 
gets the cross-model adversarial review (direct Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per 
`delegation-anthropic.md`) before it is recorded done; findings fixed or rejected with reasons in TRACK. The whole 
work-item diff gets the same review in T22.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-16-- **Test policy (BR-015, AC-036):** integration tests against 
local Supabase/Realtime/real routes and Playwright E2E only. T1–T6 run their regression E2E through the existing local 
runner (`npm run test:messaging:local:e2e`); from T24 on, every E2E gate runs through the T24 runner (local Supabase; 
real Chrome and Edge projects); no unit tests; a touched unit test is replaced and deleted, recorded in TRACK. A new 
E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing runs in Chrome and in Edge with zero retries, zero flaky, and no 
skipped critical test. Network shaping only (SPEC §15); no mocked Supabase, repositories, or code under test.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-17-- **Regression (FR-032, AC-033):** every task that changes 
server or drawer behavior ends with the messaging DB integration suite and the messaging regression E2E suite passing 
locally, plus type-check and lint.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-18-- **Presence touch points:** any change near sign-out or 
Realtime lifecycle follows the `presence-safety` skill; the Presence logout sequence is unchanged.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-19-- **Planning decisions under D4 (owner-adjustable):** budget 
infrastructure fails closed — if a create, fence, or metrics budget cannot be checked, the request is refused as a 
transient 429 (the outbox retries it) instead of being allowed; Phase 4 keyed requests that carry no attempt 
generation keep the Phase 4 keyed contract (create, replay 200, 409) and take part in the same commit-time exclusion 
as fencing: such a request commits only if no fence state exists for its key at commit time, where fence state is 
created only by a fence call or a generation-carrying request (a generation-less create creates none, so Phase 4 
retries are unaffected); a generation-less request that loses to a fence stores nothing and is rejected as stale. 
Per-stream Realtime faults in E2E may inject Phoenix channel frames (`phx_error`, `phx_close`) or withhold a single 
topic's replies on the real socket; this counts as network shaping of a single stream (SPEC §15) — the real transport, 
joins, and application callbacks stay in place and no application health is set directly; a real server mechanism is 
preferred where one exists.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-20-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-21-## Observations grounding this plan (2026-10-06, corrected 
after review r1)
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-22-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-23-- Local Supabase answers at `127.0.0.1:54321` (HTTP 200). 
Messaging DB suite `__tests__/messaging-db/*` (`vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and local E2E 
(`playwright.messaging-local.config.ts`) exist from Phase 4.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-24-- Create route (`src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts`): 
`clientMessageId` optional; repository `createWithClientKey` dedupes on unique index `(sender_id, conversation_id, 
client_message_id)` (migration `20261005000414`); the attachment path creates through a separate transactional RPC 
(route.ts:310). The Phase 4 composer sends a key for text, attachment, and voice creates (`message-composer.tsx:223`, 
`useMessages.ts:284`). No attempt generation, fence/lookup route, or expected-sender field. Early validation 
(route.ts:231) runs before any budget is charged.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-25-- Rate limiting: `enforceRateLimit` 
(`src/lib/auth/rate-limit.ts`) fails open on RPC error (line 48); `check_rate_limit` (`20260612190000`) increments a 
fixed-window counter on every call, including denied ones — an attempt counter, not a winning-insert quota.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-26-- `Message` type and feed/Realtime mappings expose no 
`clientMessageId`; optimistic matching is content/time based. Mentions do not exist.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-27-- `mark_conversation_read(uuid, uuid)` is SECURITY DEFINER, 
executable only by `service_role` since `20261004170724`, with no internal membership check; `get_unread_counts` still 
has default `anon` EXECUTE.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-28-- Typing (`src/hooks/useConversationPresence.ts`): public 
channel `conversation:{id}`; sends true once and false after 2 s idle, remote TTL 4 s; payload carries the auth uid 
and display name; on channel failure it only clears its subscribed flag (line 150).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md-29-- Realtime: `useMessageSubscription` exposes `connectionStatus` 
and backoff for the messages channel; `useConversationRealtime` exports `connectionStatus` and does catch-up on 
confirmed streams, but has no application backoff and its health is not consumed. `conversation_members` and 
`message_read_receipts` are already in the Realtime publication. No polling. No IndexedDB/BroadcastChannel; Web Locks 
only in `src/lib/messaging/desktop-notifications.ts`.
