and owner decisions D1–D6 recorded in `state.md` (Verdict: Ready).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-6-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-7-## 1. Summary
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-8-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-9-The Virtual Office messaging drawer (`MessagingDrawer` → 
`MessageFeed` → `MessageComposer` / `MessageItem`, state in `MessagingContext`, data in `useMessages` / 
`useConversations`, Realtime in `useMessageSubscription` / `useConversationRealtime`, typing in 
`useConversationPresence`) was completed for timeline features in Phase 4. Phase 4 also delivered a failed send that 
keeps text/reply/files with a single-message retry (`clientMessageId` idempotency in `POST /api/messages/create`, 
stored in `messages.client_message_id`), a Realtime catch-up after reconnect, and opt-in desktop notifications for 
DM/group messages. This phase adds: a durable per-user outbox for text messages with server-fenced attempt generations 
and safe cross-tab and cross-account behavior; a connection banner; application-level recovery and health for every 
messaging Realtime stream with polling fallback; a reliable, named, members-only typing indicator; live cross-device 
unread/read sync; @mentions with desktop notifications (including rooms); messaging health metrics as redacted server 
logs; and two Phase 4 database follow-ups plus restoring the open conversation after reload.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-10-
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-108-| FR-016 | Polling fallback: while any required stream has 
been unhealthy for more than 30 s and the tab is visible, the app fetches the open conversation's new messages, the 
receipt summaries of its loaded messages, any open reader-details list, and the conversation list every 15 s; on 
becoming visible while still unhealthy it fetches immediately, then every 15 s; no polling while hidden; once all 
streams are healthy no new polling request starts. Merging polling and Realtime results never duplicates a message and 
never replaces newer or enriched state (attachments, mentions, reactions, receipts, loaded history pages) with older 
data. | Must | AC-016, AC-048 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-109-| FR-017 | The typing indicator stays visible while the other 
person types continuously and disappears at most 5 s after they stop, blur the composer, send, leave the conversation, 
or close the tab. | Must | AC-017 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-110-| FR-018 | The indicator names typists: 1 → "Ana está 
digitando…", 2 → "Ana e Bruno estão digitando…", 3+ → "N pessoas estão digitando…", in direct, group, and room 
conversations. | Must | AC-018 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:111:| FR-019 | Typing signals travel only on a private Realtime 
topic whose join and send are authorized for current conversation members; anon clients, authenticated non-members, 
and public-topic attempts never receive them; the app detects the user's own removal from a conversation through a 
signal that does not depend on still having access to that conversation and leaves the topic within 5 s. Payload: user 
identity and typing flag only. Residual risk accepted (D3, D6): a tampered client of a removed member may receive and 
send typing signals until its access token expires. | Must | AC-019 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-112-| FR-020 | A user never sees their own typing indicator, 
including from their other tabs or devices. | Must | AC-020 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-113-| FR-021 | While connectivity and Realtime are healthy, within 
5 s and without reload, focus change, or reconnect: when the user reads messages (fully or partly) on one tab/device, 
their other tabs/devices show the same unread counts and read state, and the sender's receipt summary/details agree 
with the stored receipts on all of the sender's sessions. During an outage, FR-016 deadlines apply. | Must | AC-021 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-114-| FR-022 | While connectivity and Realtime are healthy, a 
message the user sends from one device/tab appears on their other devices/tabs within 5 s without reload; during an 
outage, FR-016 deadlines apply. | Must | AC-022 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:115:| FR-023 | In the composer, typing "@" opens a list of the 
conversation's current members except the user, filtered as they type, operable by mouse and keyboard (arrows, 
Enter/Tab, Esc); choosing inserts a highlighted mention. In a room the list contains only members of the room 
conversation. Typed "@name" text that was not chosen from the list is plain text. | Must | AC-023, AC-024 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:116:| FR-024 | On first creation the server stores mentions in the 
same transaction as the message, as application user IDs of conversation members at that time other than the sender; 
other requested IDs create no mention. The original submitted composition (content, reply target, requested mention 
IDs) is what replays are compared against: an unchanged replay returns the stored message without re-validating 
recipients; a different composition under the same key returns `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`. Clients cannot write 
mention records directly; only conversation members can read them. | Must | AC-024, AC-046 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-117-| FR-025 | With the Phase 4 desktop-notification toggle on and 
permission granted, a mentioned user receives one desktop notification for a message that mentions them (direct, 
group, room, thread reply), titled "<Autor> mencionou você em <conversa>" with the full text; clicking opens the 
conversation. Before emitting, the app confirms with authoritative data, under the current identity, that the user is 
still a member and (for rooms) mentioned; then, with no further awaits before display, it re-checks that the same user 
is still signed in and that no removal signal for that conversation has arrived; otherwise the pending notification is 
discarded, as it is on any account switch or sign-out. Residual race accepted (D6): a removal that the app has not yet 
received when the final check runs may let that one notification show. Suppression is browser-wide: no tab notifies if 
any of the user's tabs in that browser is visible and viewing that conversation, regardless of which tab receives the 
event first. | Must | AC-025, AC-026, AC-049 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-118-| FR-026 | Mentions render distinctly for everyone; a message 
that mentions the viewing user is highlighted for that user with a non-color cue. | Must | AC-027 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-119-| FR-027 | The client records metric events — send latency 
(press → server confirmed), outbox wait time, send outcomes by reason, Realtime stream drops/recoveries and outage 
duration, polling activations and duration — in a bounded buffer (oldest dropped when full) and sends them 
fire-and-forget in batches of at most 50 events and 16 KB, at most one delivery in flight, each aborted after 5 s, 
dropping batches under overload. The authenticated, per-user rate-limited route rejects oversized requests, accepts 
only closed event/reason enums and bounded numeric fields, drops anything else, adds a server-derived app version, and 
writes structured log lines under BR-013. | Must | AC-028 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-120-| FR-028 | Metrics never block, slow, or break messaging: 
messaging code never awaits metric delivery; an erroring, hanging, or overloaded metrics route changes no messaging 
behavior or timing and shows no error. | Must | AC-029 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:121:| FR-029 | `mark_conversation_read` refuses to mark a 
conversation for a user who is not a member of it. | Must | AC-030 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-122-| FR-030 | `get_unread_counts` is not executable by the `anon` 
role; authenticated use keeps working. | Must | AC-031 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-123-| FR-031 | After a page reload, if the drawer was open, it 
reopens on the same conversation for the same user on the same browser; if that conversation is no longer accessible, 
the conversation list opens without an error; a closed drawer stays closed. | Must | AC-032 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-124-| FR-032 | Existing messaging behavior (Phase 4 flows: 
receipts, attachments, voice notes, stars, DM/group notifications and their once-across-tabs claim, failed-send retry 
for attachment messages, reconnect catch-up) does not regress. | Must | AC-033 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-125-| FR-033 | When the outbox cannot be written (site storage 
unavailable or the write fails), nothing is dispatched; the text and reply target stay in the composer with the 
message "Este navegador não permite guardar mensagens; libere o armazenamento do site" (D5). | Must | AC-039 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-126-| FR-034 | Key-based correlation: the sender's representations 
of a message (outbox item, create and fence responses, feed fetches, Realtime events) carry its `clientMessageId`, and 
the feed matches pending items to stored messages only by that key, so each message shows as exactly one bubble in 
every sender tab, including identical texts and Realtime arriving before the HTTP response. | Must | AC-050 |
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-129-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-130-| ID | Rule | Rationale |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-131-|---|---|---|
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:132:| BR-001 | The outbox belongs to one application user 
(`users.id`) on one browser; it is never shown, dispatched, fenced, or deleted while another user is authenticated, 
and the server never stores or fences an item under a sender other than its owner. | R1-q3 A, R1-q16 A, R2-q5 A; 
reviews r2 #6, r3 #4 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-133-| BR-002 | Only text messages and replies without 
attachments/voice are queued. | R1-q4 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-134-| BR-003 | Per conversation, items are sent in creation order 
with at most one create request in progress across all tabs; a failed (definitive or expired) item blocks later items 
of that conversation until the user retries or deletes it. Conversations are independent. | R1-q5 A, R1-q2 E; review 
r3 #5 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-135-| BR-004 | Each item gets a stable `clientMessageId` when the 
user presses send; every attempt reuses it (except the `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` retry, FR-007); the server stores at 
most one message per (sender, conversation, `clientMessageId`), and a fenced attempt can never commit. | R1-q2 B, 
R1-q16 B; review r3 #1 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:136:| BR-005 | Outcome classes: transient = browser offline before 
dispatch, HTTP 429, HTTP 401 while the client session is valid → retry automatically; unknown = network 
error/timeout/no response after dispatch, lease expiry, HTTP 5xx → fence (FR-006); session-ended = client auth reports 
signed out / refresh rejected → hold (FR-012); definitive = 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (incl. a missing conversation), 400 
(e.g. `INVALID_REPLY_TARGET`), 413 `CONTENT_TOO_LARGE`, 409 `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`, sender mismatch, and any other 
4xx except 401/429 → failed, no automatic retry; a stale-generation rejection only means a newer attempt exists and is 
ignored (FR-011). | R1-q5 C, R2-q4 A, R2-q5 A; reviews r2 #2, #11 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-137-| BR-006 | Expiry: an item not stored 24 h after the user 
pressed send (or after its last manual "Tentar de novo") becomes "expirada" and is never sent automatically; a manual 
"Tentar de novo" sends it with the same key and starts a new 24 h window. | R1-q5 D, R2-q3 B |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:138:| BR-007 | Cancel only for items known not to be stored, with 
no earlier attempt able to commit, and not claimed; a cancelled item is removed in all tabs and never dispatched. | 
R1-q5 B, R2-q7 A; reviews r2 #2, #5, r3 #1 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-139-| BR-008 | An explicit user sign-out with unsent items 
requires confirmation; confirming deletes that user's outbox; a sign-out not initiated by the user keeps it. 
Cancelling has no side effect. | R2-q5 A, R2-q6 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:140:| BR-009 | Typing: only current conversation members join and 
send on a conversation's typing topic; a user's own typing (any session) is never shown to them; an indicator expires 
≤ 5 s after the last signal; the app leaves a conversation's topic within 5 s of the user's removal; residual exposure 
(receive and send) of a tampered removed-member client is bounded by access-token lifetime (D3, D6). | R1-q8 A, D, E; 
R1-q16 E; D3; D6 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:141:| BR-010 | Mentions: only current members of the conversation 
at first creation, other than the sender, can be mentioned (rooms: members of the room conversation); no 
`@todos`/`@here`. | R1-q10 A, E; R2-q10 A; D4 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:142:| BR-011 | Desktop-notification eligibility (extends Phase 4): 
toggle on and permission granted; never for the user's own message; the same user must still be signed in and a member 
at emission time (final check without intervening awaits; residual race accepted, D6); never while any tab of the user 
in that browser is visible and viewing that conversation; DM/group: every new message; room: only messages that 
mention the user; at most one notification per message per browser. | R1-q10 B, R1-q16 C/F, R2-q8 A, R2-q9 A–C; 
reviews r2 #9, r3 #3 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-143-| BR-012 | Polling runs only while a required Realtime stream 
has been unhealthy for more than 30 s and the tab is visible, every 15 s (immediately on becoming visible), and no new 
poll starts once all streams are healthy. | R1-q7 A, R1-q16 D, R2-q12 C |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:144:| BR-013 | Metric log lines contain only closed-enum event 
type and outcome/reason, bounded durations/counts, conversation type, timestamp, and server-derived app version — 
never message text, attachment names, conversation names, user names or emails, user/conversation identifiers, or any 
client-supplied free text. | R1-q12 B, R2-q2, confirmation point 9; review r2 #14 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-145-| BR-014 | Database rollout: migrations stay local during the 
phase (written + applied locally with recorded rollback SQL); at phase end they are applied to `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` 
only with explicit owner authorization, followed by catalog readback and a runtime smoke check; the application is 
deployed by the owner after the migrations; rollback is app first, then migrations. | R1-q13 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-146-| BR-015 | Tests: only integration (real local 
Supabase/Realtime/API routes) and E2E (real UI, Playwright); no new unit tests; a touched unit test is replaced by 
integration/E2E coverage and deleted, recorded in TRACK. Each new E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing 
runs. | AGENTS.md test policy, R2-q13 A |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-147-| BR-016 | Conversation restore is per browser and per user; a 
different user never inherits it. | R2-q11 A, B, D |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-148-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-149-## 9. Data and integrations
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-211-| Stale poll returns after a newer Realtime update | 
Newer/enriched state kept; no duplicates (AC-048). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-212-| Realtime down > 30 s, tab hidden | No polling; on visible, 
fetch immediately then every 15 s (AC-016). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-213-| Typist closes the tab or leaves the conversation mid-typing 
| Indicator disappears ≤ 5 s (AC-017). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:214:| Anon, outsider, public-topic, or removed-member typing 
access | Refused / no events; removed member's app leaves at once; tampered client bounded by D3 (AC-019). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:215:| Forged mention IDs, plain "@name", changed mentions on 
replay, recipient removed before replay | No mention for non-members/self/plain text; changed composition → 409; 
unchanged replay returns the stored message (AC-024, AC-046). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-216-| Recipient removed or account switched after commit but 
before the notification is shown | No notification once the app has the removal/switch signal; a removal not yet 
received at the final check is the accepted D6 race (AC-049). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-217-| Manual retry of an expired item hits 429 or an unknown 
outcome | New 24 h window: retried/fenced automatically (AC-010). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-218-| Partial reads by others during a Realtime-only outage | 
Receipt summaries and open reader details update via polling (AC-016). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-219-| Hidden tab receives a mention event first while another tab 
views that conversation | No notification (AC-026). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-220-| Malicious, oversized, hanging, or sustained metrics traffic 
| Rejected or dropped; route rate-limited; messaging unaffected (AC-028, AC-029). |
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-259-- AC-016 (FR-016, BR-012; must-not R1-q16 D): Given Realtime 
is blocked while HTTP works and A's tab is visible, when B sends a message at the outage start, then A sees it within 
45 s; a message B sends after polling started appears within 15 s plus request time; the list's unread counts update; 
when C reads part of A's earlier messages during the outage (no new message sent), A's receipt summaries and open 
reader-details list update within 15 s plus request time once polling is active. Given only the conversation-list 
stream is unhealthy for more than 30 s, polling starts too. When A's tab is hidden, no polling requests are made; when 
it becomes visible, a fetch happens immediately. When Realtime recovers while a poll is in flight, the message 
delivered by both appears once, and no new polling request starts during the next 60 s.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-260-- AC-017 (FR-017; must-not R1-q16 E): Given B types 
continuously for 15 s, then A sees the typing indicator at every 1 s sample; when B stops, it disappears within 5 s; 
when B closes the tab mid-typing, within 5 s; when B switches to another conversation mid-typing, within 5 s.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-261-- AC-018 (FR-018): Given a group or room with A, B, C, D, when 
B types, A sees "<B> está digitando…"; B and C → "<B> e <C> estão digitando…"; B, C, D → "3 pessoas estão digitando…"; 
a direct conversation shows the single-typist phrase.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:262:- AC-019 (FR-019, BR-009): With real local Realtime: an anon 
client, an authenticated non-member, and a client on the public topic name receive no typing events of conversation X 
and cannot send typing events members receive; member A receives B's typing; when member E is removed from X while 
subscribed (and while X is not open in E's drawer), E's app leaves the topic within 5 s and shows no further typing 
for X (integration + E2E).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:263:- AC-020 (FR-020, BR-009): Given A has two tabs and a second 
device on X, when A types in tab 1, then neither tab 2 nor the second device shows A as typing.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-264-- AC-021 (FR-021): Given healthy connectivity and A on two 
devices with 6 unread in X, when A reads only the first 3 on device 1, then within 5 s device 2 shows 3 unread for X; 
after reading the rest, 0. Given A is the sender of messages read by B, then A's receipt summary/details on both of 
A's sessions match the stored receipts within 5 s.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-265-- AC-022 (FR-022): Given healthy connectivity and A on two 
devices, when A sends on device 1, then it appears once on device 2 within 5 s without reload.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:266:- AC-023 (FR-023, BR-010): Given A types "@" in a room 
conversation, then the list shows only room-conversation members other than A, filters as A types, and supports 
arrows/Enter/Tab/Esc and mouse; choosing "Bruno" inserts a highlighted mention; a workspace user who never joined the 
room chat is not listed.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:267:- AC-024 (FR-023, FR-024, BR-010; must-not R1-q16 F): On the 
real route and local DB: a message mentioning a non-member ID and the sender's own ID stores no mention for either and 
notifies neither; a replay that changes only the requested mention IDs returns `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` and changes 
nothing; a message whose text contains "@Bruno" typed without selection stores no mention; a forced failure of mention 
storage stores neither the message nor any mention; anon and non-members cannot read mention records; no client can 
insert/update/delete them directly.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-268-- AC-025 (FR-025, BR-011): Given B has notifications enabled 
and permission granted, B's tab hidden or viewing another conversation, when A mentions B in a room, then B receives 
exactly one notification "<A> mencionou você em <sala>" with the full text; clicking opens that room in the drawer; a 
room message without a mention of B produces none.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-269-- AC-026 (FR-025, BR-011; must-not R1-q16 C): Given B has 
notifications enabled, then a DM mention yields exactly one notification; a thread-reply mention yields one; with B's 
two tabs where the hidden tab receives the event first and the visible tab is viewing that conversation, none; A's own 
message yields none for A; with the toggle off, none; a mention across B's two hidden tabs yields exactly one.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-270-- AC-027 (FR-026): Given A's message mentions B, then all 
members see the mention styled distinctly, and only B sees the whole message highlighted with a non-color cue.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-271-- AC-028 (FR-027, BR-013): Given a send, a stream recovery, 
and a polling episode occur, then the metrics route writes structured lines with enum event type/reason, durations, 
and server-derived version; a scan finds no message text, names, emails, or user/conversation IDs; a payload with 
unknown fields, free-text strings, out-of-range numbers, or a forged version produces no such values in the logs; a 
request over 50 events or 16 KB is rejected; requests beyond the per-user rate limit are rejected; an unauthenticated 
request is rejected and produces no metric log line.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-272-- AC-029 (FR-028): Given the metrics route errors, and 
separately hangs, and separately is flooded with sustained traffic, when A sends, goes offline, and reconnects, then 
AC-001/AC-002 behavior and timing hold, at most one metrics request is in flight from A's tab, a hanging metrics 
request is aborted after 5 s, the client buffer never exceeds its bound (oldest events dropped), and no error is shown.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:273:- AC-030 (FR-029): Given user E is not a member of X, when 
`mark_conversation_read` is invoked for E and X through every role that can execute it, then the call is refused and 
E's read state for X is unchanged (integration, local DB).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-274-- AC-031 (FR-030): Given the `anon` role, when it calls 
`get_unread_counts`, then permission is denied; an authenticated member still gets correct counts (integration, local 
DB).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-275-- AC-032 (FR-031, BR-016): Given the drawer open on X, when A 
reloads, then it reopens on X; given A lost access to X, then the list opens with no error; given C signs in on that 
browser, then C does not get A's conversation; given the drawer was closed, it stays closed.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-276-- AC-033 (FR-032): The existing Phase 4 messaging E2E 
regression suite and DB integration suite pass after each slice; `npm run type-check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run 
